    anything holds `globalThis`; JSContextGetGlobalObject returns the new proxy. */
 JS_EXPORT void JSGlobalContextInstallNamedProperties(JSGlobalContextRef ctx, JSNamedPropertyFilter filter, JSObjectGetPropertyCallback getter);
 
+/* Makes the global object of `ctx` the target of `proxy`, the global proxy of another
+   context of the same group (what JSContextGetGlobalObject returned there): a WindowProxy
+   that follows its browsing context to the next document. From then on `proxy` is the
+   `this`, `globalThis` and JSContextGetGlobalObject of `ctx`, and every reference to it,
+   also in the other context, reaches the global object of `ctx`. Call on a new context,
+   after JSGlobalContextInstallNamedProperties and before any of its code is compiled
+   (optimized code may hold the proxy a global had). Returns false, changing nothing,
+   when `proxy` is not a global proxy of this VM. */
+JS_EXPORT bool JSGlobalContextAdoptGlobalProxy(JSGlobalContextRef ctx, JSObjectRef proxy);
